{"name":"Moth Grey","hex":"#dad3cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any flying insect of the order Lepidoptera not in the superfamily Papilionoidea, most species of which are nocturnal and can be distinguished from butterflies by feather-like antennae.","Anything that gradually and silently eats, consumes, or wastes any other thing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt for moths."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moth"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moth","blocks":[{"text":"Moths are a group of winged insects of the order Lepidoptera, the other well-known members of which are butterflies; they are characterized by dark or dull patterned wings. They were previously classified as suborder Heterocera, but the group is paraphyletic with respect to butterflies and neither subordinate taxon is used in modern classifications. Moths make up the vast majority of the order. There are approximately 160,000 species of moth, many of which have yet to be described. Most species of moth are nocturnal, although there are also crepuscular and diurnal species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Autographa_gamma_en_Trachelospermum_jasminoides_-_02.jpg/330px-Autographa_gamma_en_Trachelospermum_jasminoides_-_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moth","wikidata":"Q1725788"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Arctia_caja_525.jpg/500px-Arctia_caja_525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Arctia_caja_525.jpg/1280px-Arctia_caja_525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Arctia_caja_525.jpg/500px-Arctia_caja_525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArctia_caja_525.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg/500px-Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg/1280px-Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg/500px-Spilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ardices canescens, eating a leaf","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpilosoma_canescens_caterpillar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Curoba_sangarida_Moth_15_Pupa_%282015.11.13%29.jpg/500px-Curoba_sangarida_Moth_15_Pupa_%282015.11.13%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu